  First off, I have not posted many messages here, but I do read most of the
messages.  And I must say, that this topic of polypiling has been a L  O  N  G
running one.  But, a few messages back, I saw what I think to be the best
answer to this problem (I think it was Jef Poskanzer <my apologies for
spelling>).  Why not limit the number of items you can put in one space.  It
would seem logical that you would not be able to pile 250 items into a one foot
square space...just let say 4 or maybe 5 items (depending on size if you go for
realism) sit on one spot and have all the others role off in different
directions.

  Just a thought.


